<title>RUSSIA: Russia to offer 10.50 trln rbls in paper Oct 23.</title>
<headline>Russia to offer 10.50 trln rbls in paper Oct 23.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian finance ministry will offer eight trillion roubles in six-month GKO discount Treasury bills and 2.50 trillion roubles in two-year OFZ interest-bearing bonds on October 23, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow.</p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		     22055</p>
<p>    Issue volume			8.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				 182 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     April 23, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		     24009</p>
<p>    Issue volume			2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				 728 days</p>
<p>    First coupon date		 Jan 22, 1997</p>
<p>    First coupon (annual rate)    42.78 pct</p>
<p>    Second coupon date		April 23, 1997</p>
<p>    Third coupon date		 July 23, 1997</p>
<p>    Fourth coupon date		Oct 22, 1997</p>
<p>    Fifth coupon date		 Jan 21, 1998</p>
<p>    Sixth coupon date		 April 22, 1998</p>
<p>    Seventh coupon date	     July 22, 1998</p>
<p>    Eighth coupon date		Oct 21, 1998</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     Oct 21, 1998</p>
<p>NOTE - The volume of the first coupon on the bond in cash terms is 106.657 roubles.</p>
<p>On October 23, the finance ministry will repay about 6.73 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bill (series 22030).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
